---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<Layout title="How to join – EuCAIF">
<Nav />

<section class="page-header">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="section-label">How to join</div>
    <h1 class="section-title">Participating in EuCAIF</h1>
    <p class="section-desc">
      EuCAIF is establishing a network of researchers across European institutions to bridge fundamental physics
      and AI research. The network connects leading scientists who visibly advance both fields, provide scientific
      leadership to the community in Europe, and train the next generation to drive this transformative work forward.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tiers-section">
  <div class="section-container">
    <p class="section-desc">There are three levels of involvement in EuCAIF.</p>
    <div class="tiers-grid">
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-level">Level 1</div>
        <h3>Members</h3>
        <p>
          Anyone may become a EuCAIF member by subscribing to the <strong>eucaif-info</strong> mailing list.
          Membership is intended as an open and lightweight way to stay connected with EuCAIF.
        </p>
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="/eucaif.org/contact/">Subscribe via CERN e-groups</a>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card">
        <div class="tier-level">Level 2</div>
        <h3>Junior Fellows</h3>
        <p>
          Scientists at advanced early-career stages, typically tenure-track or equivalent, who do not yet hold a
          tenured or permanent position at a European institution, who are on a trajectory toward such positions,
          and who demonstrate strong engagement with EuCAIF's mission.
        </p>
        <p>
          The same four criteria as for fellows apply, assessed relative to career stage: evidence of potential may
          substitute for a full track record in training young scientists or providing scientific leadership.
          Junior fellows automatically transition to fellows upon obtaining a tenured or equivalent permanent position
          at a European institution. Applications follow the fellowship procedure below.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-card tier-card-accent">
        <div class="tier-level">Level 3</div>
        <h3>Fellows</h3>
        <p>
          Fellows guide the strategic direction of EuCAIF, contribute actively to the implementation of its
          activities, and participate in regular meetings to take key decisions, including the election of
          Management Board members.
        </p>
        <p>
          Scientists holding permanent scientific positions at European institutions, or equivalent long-term
          appointments, with a strong track record and high visibility in AI and fundamental physics may apply for
          a renewable five-year fellowship.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="prose-section">
  <div class="section-container prose">
    <div class="section-label">Fellowship criteria</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Requirements</h2>
    <p>
      EuCAIF follows the broad definition of "Europe" used by JENAA and its supporting organisations
      (ECFA, NuPECC and APPEC), which serves as the reference for eligibility. Specific requirements include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Internationally recognized, high-impact publications in their research field</li>
      <li>High-impact publications on AI methods relevant to fundamental physics, in either AI or physics venues</li>
      <li>A demonstrable track record of training young scientists advancing AI in fundamental physics</li>
      <li>Active and leading contributions to EuCAIF activities as a member, or a clear plan for such contributions presented in the application</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Exceptional candidates who do not yet meet all criteria may still be considered.</p>

    <div class="section-label" style="margin-top: 3rem;">Application procedure</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">How to apply</h2>
    <p>
      Fellowship applications should be sent to the management board at
      <a href="mailto:info@eucaif.org">info@eucaif.org</a> and consist of a short expression of interest
      (maximum half a page, excluding references) outlining how the applicant envisions contributing to EuCAIF and
      how they have contributed in the past to AI in fundamental physics.
    </p>
    <p>
      Applications are reviewed by three independent referees selected by the Management Board: one from the
      candidate's field, one from a related field, and one Management Board member. Final decisions are made by
      majority vote of all Management Board members.
    </p>
    <p>
      Full details can be found in the <a href="/eucaif.org/documents/EuCAIF-policy-v0.7.pdf">EuCAIF policy document</a>,
      also listed on the <a href="/eucaif.org/material/">material page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<Footer />
</Layout>
